          "settings": {
            "category": "Implementation & Deployment",
            "question": "How do you handle partial deployments and expansion?",
            "answer": "Flow is designed for incremental deployment. Start with high-value zones (fitting rooms, checkout, featured displays) then expand. Each zone operates independently—no requirement to deploy store-wide. Zone-level licensing available. Common approach: Phase 1 (2-4 weeks) = 3-5 priority zones. Phase 2 (4-8 weeks) = expand to full floor coverage. Phase 3 (ongoing) = add stockroom, entrance, or seasonal zones as needed. Configuration and insights transfer between zones—no re-training. Multi-store rollouts follow the same pattern: pilot store proves ROI, then standardized deployment to additional locations.",
