          "settings": {
            "category": "Accuracy & Data Quality",
            "question": "What does '98.5% accuracy' mean in operational terms?",
            "answer": "98.5% is our people-counting accuracy measured against manual ground truth counts in production environments. Operationally: In a store with 1,000 daily visitors, expect ~15 count variance. Accuracy is measured per camera view, not per person—crossed paths and occlusions are handled. Accuracy holds across lighting conditions, crowd density, and demographic diversity. Dwell time accuracy: ±3 seconds for sessions under 2 minutes. Zone transition accuracy: 97.2% (person moving between zones correctly tracked). Heatmap spatial accuracy: 30cm grid resolution. Conversion tracking accuracy: 99.1% when POS integration is enabled (compares Flow visit count to POS transaction count). We provide weekly accuracy reports with sample imagery for validation.",
