        "ai_gen_block_0c78d27_cAnRTW": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_0c78d27",
          "name": "FAQ accordion item",
          "settings": {
            "category": "Accuracy & Data Quality",
            "question": "How do you handle edge cases: children, groups, staff, after-hours?",
            "answer": "Children: Tracked if height >90cm (typical 3-year-old). Strollers counted as +1 if occupied. Groups: Each individual counted separately—Flow tracks group movement patterns but reports per-person metrics. Staff: Identified by (1) time-of-day patterns, (2) zone access (staff-only areas), or (3) badge integration if available. Staff metrics separated from customer metrics. After-hours: Cleaning crews and restocking automatically filtered by time-based rules (configurable threshold, e.g., <5 people after closing = staff mode). Manual override available. Delivery personnel: Brief visits (<2 min) auto-classified as non-customer. All edge cases appear in audit log—review and adjust classification rules as needed.",
