          "settings": {
            "category": "Accuracy & Data Quality",
            "question": "What happens during system downtime or camera obstructions?",
            "answer": "Edge processing provides resilience: cameras store up to 24 hours of data locally if internet fails. Data syncs when connection restores—no data loss. Obstructions (e.g., maintenance ladder blocking camera): Flow detects coverage gaps and flags affected zones in real-time. Historical data marked as 'partial coverage'—reports indicate data quality per zone per hour. Scheduled maintenance: Set cameras to 'maintenance mode' to suppress alerts. Unplanned outages: System auto-detects and logs. Camera failure: Redundant coverage design means adjacent cameras provide fallback data (lower resolution). SLA: 99.9% uptime measured monthly. Downtime notifications sent via email/SMS to designated contacts.",
            "default_open": false,
